From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Majewski <mail@martinmajewski.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:46:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mac launcher: bring the last-played save along, all or
 nothing, and fall back on HFS+

Patch 0112 keeps a game's save in ~/Library when its game library folder
is on a drive that can't hold saves. Review of #920 found three ways it
still loses progress:

- A volume move could start the game on an older save. 0112 copied a
  save only into an empty folder, so an older copy left in ~/Library
  (or in the library folder) won over the newer one. The launcher now
  writes the folder it started the game from to <id>/save-location and
  brings that whole save along when the folder changes. Without a
  record, the library's save counts as current, since every build since
  patch 0010 played from it. A library save folder holding only
  .DS_Store or ._ files counts as empty.
- A copy that failed halfway was reported as done, and the game started
  on half a save without ever retrying. The save is now copied into
  <save>.migrating and renamed into place only when every file arrived.
  An older save in the destination is kept as <save>.replaced-<time>,
  never merged file by file. If the copy fails, an alert says why, the
  game doesn't start, both folders stay as they were, and the next
  start tries again.
- HFS+ leaves the clone and swap bits out of its valid mask, so 0112
  treated it as able to hold saves. When a volume doesn't report them,
  the filesystem name from statfs now decides, and only apfs keeps
  saves beside the app.

The device save beside a save (<save>_device, hle_fs.c) moves together
with it. A save folder the launch environment sets (DM_SAVE, which the
launcher can now pick) is used as it is and only recorded, so a later
start without it brings that save along.

Tests in test_nsp_mac_app.App, each failing on 0112:
test_library_folder_on_hfs, test_library_save_beats_older_home_save,
test_library_back_on_apfs (with a device save),
test_library_save_copy_fails (a copy cut short by a file-size limit),
test_library_save_chosen_by_the_front_end and
test_library_folder_on_apfs (the record). The exFAT test moves into a
helper shared with HFS+, and test_library_save_folder_with_only_finder_files
covers the Finder files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending (a fix to patch 0112, which only this fork has; upstream's version of the feature is seedds/nxnative#460)
Reason: Patch 0112 loses progress when a game library moves between drives, when a save copy fails halfway, or on HFS+
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#920

